      <marc:subfield code="a">“Ghost Clap” is a full-length novel by Jiang Taiyu, written with a touch of humor after personally investigating haunted houses across Taiwan. It marks his first venture into the thriller and suspense genre. Behind the horror and the supernatural lies a deeper exploration of the kind of evil that often escapes punishment in the living world—stories of longing, love, and greed that lead to joy, sorrow, and separation. The novel is also filled with warmth, laughter, and tears</marc:subfield>
